From: SP11 Linux audio parity project
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: defer integrated pull backend config

The first audio-v3 boot proves that DPCM backend prepare reaches the shared
graph before frontend prepare. The backend therefore sends PCM/MFC and
protection configuration before the pull ring and module events exist. The
DSP rejects that out-of-order SET_CFG with status 1.

The recovered Windows transaction has a single configuration owner. It
configures the pull ring and events first, followed by pull/PCM/MFC formats
and the protection tail. The integrated Linux frontend now implements that
complete order.

Skip generic backend configuration only when the topology is the protected
pull graph. Existing split AudioReach graphs retain their current backend
prepare behavior.

---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
@@ -215,6 +215,20 @@
 		dai_data->graph[dai->id] = graph;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The integrated SP11 pull graph has one Windows-ordered configuration
+	 * owner: its frontend.  Generic backend prepare runs first in the DPCM
+	 * sequence, before the pull ring and event registrations exist.  Sending
+	 * PCM/MFC/protection configuration here therefore changes the captured
+	 * order and is rejected by the DSP.  The frontend configures the same
+	 * shared graph completely before start.
+	 */
+	if (dai_data->graph[dai->id]->pull_mode) {
+		dev_info_once(dai->dev,
+			      "SP11 pull graph: backend configuration deferred to frontend\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	cfg->direction = substream->stream;
 	rc = q6apm_graph_media_format_pcm(dai_data->graph[dai->id], cfg);
 	if (rc) {
